### 4\. How the gadget screen should work in your game

Use a grid with four tabs:

| Tab          | What it contains                             |
| ------------ | -------------------------------------------- |
| Travel       | Anywhere Door, Time Machine                  |
| Movement     | Bamboo Copter and other movement gadgets     |
| Object tools | Small Light, Big Light, Time Cloth           |
| Information  | Translation Konjac, Time TV, finding devices |

When the player taps a gadget, open a detail panel containing:

* Gadget illustration

* Official or selected name

* Short explanation

* How to activate it

* Compatible objects in the current room

* A Use button

* A hint if it cannot currently be used

For your first prototype, implement only three functional gadgets: one that reveals clues, one that changes an object's size, and one that unlocks travel between rooms. Add more after the core puzzle system works.

